note: Fields of a kind with variants need the variant checked first.
a shape is one of:
    a circle with a radius (a number).
    a rectangle with a width (a number) and a height (a number).
    a square with a width (a number).
    a point.

let shapes be a list of (a new point), (a new circle with radius 1).
let s be item 1 of shapes.
say s's radius.
say s's width.
say (item 2 of shapes)'s radius.
if s is a rectangle:
    say s's radius.
set s's radius to 4.
say s's colour.
say s's radios.
let p be a new circle.
let q be a new circle with radius 1 and radius 2.
let r be a new point with size 2.
let t be a new circle with radius "big".
let n be 5.
if n is a circle, say 1.
keep unit as a new point.
keep round as s is a circle.
